Notice ID               :         144738
Notice Type ID          :         RESERVE NOTICE
Notice Type Description :         LRC/LOR1/LOR2/LOR3
Issue Date              :         04/08/2026
External Reference      :         RESERVE NOTICE MT PASA 4 August 2026

-------------------------------------------------------------------

Reason :

The MTPASA result published on 4 August 2026 identifies annual unserved energy exceeds the Reliability Standard between:
-- August 2027 - August 2028 in South Australia  
-- August 2027 - August 2028 in Victoria
 
AEMO declares Low Reserve Conditions in accordance with clause 4.8.4 of the National Electricity Rules (NER) for the following region(s) and periods:
-- July 2028 in South Australia
-- July 2028 in Victoria
when forecast demand exceeds supply under some circumstances.
 
MTPASA considers transmission augmentations only once they near commissioning and applies participants submitted planned outages and weekly energy limits.
 
As a result, future transmission augmentations, including Project EnergyConnect Stage 2 and other planned network developments, are incorporated into MTPASA only as they approach commissioning. Once included, these augmentations are expected to improve the ability to share resources between regions, which may reduce forecast reliability risks.  
 
MTPASA therefore may identify greater levels of reliability risk than identified in the Electricity Statement of Opportunities.


MTPASA informs the market of potential reliability issues to allow the market to respond in the first instance, potentially avoiding the need for any AEMO intervention. 

For further information on MT PASA, please refer to:
https://www.aemo.com.au/Electricity/National-Electricity-Market-NEM/Data/Market-Management-System-MMS/Projected-Assessment-of-System-Adequacy.

For more information about how AEMO implements the reliability standard, please view the Reliability Standard Implementation Guidelines (RSIG) available on AEMO's website at https://www.aemo.com.au/energy-systems/electricity/national-electricity-market-nem/nem-forecasting-and-planning/forecasting-and-reliability/reliability-standard-implementation-guidelines.

This notice supersedes Market Notice 144649 published on 28 July 2026.

Forecasting

AEMO

